<% content_for :title, "Delete Your Account · BiblioRata" %>
<div class="ps-root ps-tut-root">
  <div class="ps-tut">
    <header class="ps-tut-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">&#9769; &nbsp; BiblioRata &nbsp; &#9769;</div>
      <h1>Delete your BiblioRata account</h1>
      <p class="lede">How to permanently delete your BiblioRata account and the data in it.</p>
      <div class="ps-tut-hero-cta">
        <%= link_to "Back to your desk", root_path, class: "cta secondary" %>
        <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path, class: "cta secondary" %>
      </div>
    </header>

    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-16 text-[17px] leading-relaxed">
      <p>This page is for the BiblioRata app on Android and iPhone and the website at
         bibliorata.com. They share one account, so deleting it in one place deletes it
         everywhere.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Delete it yourself (takes a minute)</h2>
      <ol class="ml-6 list-decimal">
        <li><strong>In the app:</strong> open the <strong>More</strong> tab and tap
            <strong>Account</strong>. <strong>On the web:</strong> sign in and go to
            <%= link_to "bibliorata.com/account", account_url %>.</li>
        <li>Under <strong>Delete my account</strong>, type your password.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Delete my account</strong> and confirm.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4">Your account is deleted straight away. If you want a copy first, use
         <strong>Download my data</strong> on the same page.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Can&rsquo;t sign in? Ask us</h2>
      <p>Email <%= mail_to LegalController.contact_email, nil,
           subject: "Delete my BiblioRata account" %> from the email address you signed up with,
         with the subject &ldquo;Delete my BiblioRata account&rdquo;. We will delete the account
         and confirm by email within 30 days. We may ask you to confirm the request from that
         address before we delete anything.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">What is deleted</h2>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
        <li>Your account: email address and password.</li>
        <li>Your studies, notes, highlights, reading plans, plan progress and reflections.</li>
        <li>Your preach queues and any pictures you uploaded for them.</li>
        <li>Your live sessions and shared-study links (shared links stop working).</li>
        <li>Your sign-in sessions, AI usage counters, and any testimonials or ratings you left.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">What may be kept, and for how long</h2>
      <p>Copies in our backups are overwritten within a limited time, and server logs (IP
         addresses and pages requested) are kept for a short period for security. Neither is used
         to restore your account. Bibles you downloaded for offline reading stay on your device
         until you remove them in the app or uninstall it.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
